From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: lethalbas <lethalbas@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 27 Nov 2026 19:55:42 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] build(ecc): raise YYINITDEPTH to 1000 for bison 3.8

With bison 3.8.2 the Ecc parser cannot relocate its stack because
YYSTYPE (SType) is a non-trivial C++ type, so it stops at the default
YYINITDEPTH of 200 and fails on Entities/Player.es(5589) with
'memory exhausted'. tx00100xt/SeriousSamClassic-VK uses the same
'#define YYINITDEPTH 1000' in Ecc/Parser.y.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 Sources/Ecc/Parser.y | 4 ++++
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+)

diff --git a/Sources/Ecc/Parser.y b/Sources/Ecc/Parser.y
index 977882b611040f5abdc376758ed19f435f04f266..4085c1b6db7e6db24bc9f50515b31b8de5486eaa 100644
--- a/Sources/Ecc/Parser.y
+++ b/Sources/Ecc/Parser.y
@@ -3,6 +3,10 @@
 #include "Ecc/StdH.h"
 #include "Ecc/Main.h"
 
+// SSTRE: bison >= 3 cannot grow the parser stack for a non-trivial C++ YYSTYPE;
+// use a larger initial stack (same value as tx00100xt/SeriousSamClassic-VK Ecc/Parser.y).
+#define YYINITDEPTH 1000
+
 static char *_strCurrentClass;
 static int _iCurrentClassID;
 static char *_strCurrentBase;
